{
  "_doc": "Outfits by category (docs/OUTFIT-BASE.md). Each worn look = the category base of its armour's style, then the style, then the armour item (top and trousers), plus the boots, gloves and helm items, each shaped after its item icon. Bases are built from the body (src/render/base-garments.js): a top shell (torso and arms, `offset` m out), a skirt (a flared ring from the waist, weights blended into the thighs), boot shafts and gloves (lower legs and hands, also body shells). Merging is src/core/outfit-look.js resolveOutfit. palette: hex colours or \"$tunic\" (the chosen tunic colour). cut (top): sleeve/cuff 0..1 shoulder to wrist (sleeve 0 = sleeveless, >1 full), hem m below the hips (<= 0.16), trim piping width, panel front placket half width, yoke depth below the neck, stripe sleeve stripe half width, neck V depth (m), pants 0..1 hips to ankle where the trousers end, pattern 0 none / 1 bands / 2 dots / 3 plate segments. skirt: length (m below the waist), flare (m at the hem), opening (radians either side of the front, 0 = closed). boots/gloves: len (boots 0..1 ankle to knee, >1 above it; gloves 0..1 of the forearm above the wrist), pattern, palette main/trim/accent/sole. helms: kind (a headwear builder in src/render/headwear.js) and palette. parts: names in src/render/outfit.js PARTS (top, boot and glove parts) ; `drop` removes inherited parts.",
